pcm: do not test an unread event value in poll_revents

Under PulseAudio 16.1 (module-alsa-sink, tsched=0) bluealsa_poll_revents() is
entered with POLLIN set while the eventfd is already drained, about 11 times a
minute on a comma 3X. eventfd_read() then fails with EAGAIN and the
uninitialized value was tested for the 0xDEAD0000 marker, so stack garbage made
the plugin report the PCM as disconnected (-ENODEV) every few minutes while
audio was flowing. Measured on device: 8 false disconnects in 20 minutes
before, 0 in 12 minutes with 142 failed reads after.

diff --git a/src/asound/bluealsa-pcm.c b/src/asound/bluealsa-pcm.c
index 3aee1cb..daa944d 100644
--- a/src/asound/bluealsa-pcm.c
+++ b/src/asound/bluealsa-pcm.c
@@ -1377,7 +1377,7 @@ static int bluealsa_poll_revents(snd_pcm_ioplug_t *io, struct pollfd *pfd,
 
 	if (pfd[0].revents & POLLIN) {
 
-		eventfd_t event;
+		eventfd_t event = 0;
 		eventfd_read(pcm->event_fd, &event);
 
 		if (event & 0xDEAD0000)
